NGINX Docker Container Setup on Application Server 3
This document provides a complete guide and walkthrough for setting up an NGINX-based container on Application Server 3 in the Stratos Datacenter as part of the Nautilus DevOps team requirements.

Task Requirements
Target Server: Application Server 3 (stapp03)

Task Details:

Pull the nginx:alpine Docker image.

Create a container named apps using the pulled image.

Map host port 8086 to container port 80 and ensure the container remains running.

Step-by-Step Execution Guide
1. Connect to Application Server 3
SSH into Application Server 3 from the jump host using the credentials for user banner:

Bash
ssh banner@stapp03
Password: BigGr33n

2. Pull the NGINX Alpine Image
Download the lightweight nginx:alpine image from Docker Hub:

Bash
docker pull nginx:alpine
3. Run and Configure the Container
Create and start the container named apps, mapping port 8086 on the host to port 80 inside the container in detached mode:

Bash
docker run -d --name apps -p 8086:80 nginx:alpine
